## 1. Data Protection (GDPR)

### 1.1 Legal basis register

[FILL: For each processing activity, list the GDPR Art.6 legal basis (consent / contract / legal-obligation / vital-interest / public-task / legitimate-interest). Include the data category and the retention period.]

### 1.2 Right to erasure (Art. 17)

[FILL: Document the cascade for an erasure request. The cascade must enumerate every system that holds the user's data, including third-party processors. Use the M-05 erasure-runbook template (see governance/gdpr-erasure-runbook.md once #713 lands) for the orchestration detail. Pay special attention to systems where the user record is DISABLED rather than DELETED — those are incomplete Art.17 compliance.]

### 1.3 Security of processing (Art. 32)

[FILL: For each system in the legal-basis register, document the technical and organisational measures. Minimum surface: encryption at rest + in transit, access logging, key-rotation cadence, incident-response runbook reference, breach-notification path.]

### 1.4 Data subject access (Art. 15)

[FILL: SLA for access requests + the system that exports the data + format(s) supported. Include the human reviewer step before release.]

